        <td id="descriptionArea">
            <h3><a name="Description"></a>Description</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Users can log in using new authentication options:
	<ul>
		<li>"Sign in using SSO"</li>
		<li>"Sign in with Passkey"</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
	<li>These appear below the existing "Sign in with Google" button on the login page.</li>
	<li>Both options should provide a seamless, secure login experience.</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="AcceptanceCriteria"></a>Acceptance Criteria</h3>

<ol>
	<li>Both new login buttons are visible and placed below "Sign in with Google."</li>
	<li>SSO login authenticates users correctly and handles errors.</li>
	<li>Passkey login authenticates users when registered; fallback guidance if no passkey is available.</li>
	<li>Proper error messages for failed authentications and unsupported devices.</li>
	<li>Compatibility with supported browsers/devices and identity providers.</li>
	<li>Security protocols followed (OAuth/SAML/WebAuthn).</li>
</ol>


<h3><a name="OutofScope"></a>Out of Scope</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Passkey registration flow</li>
	<li>SSO provider configuration</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="TestScenarios"></a>Test Scenarios</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Verify button visibility and position</li>
	<li>Validate successful and failed SSO login</li>
	<li>Validate passkey login and fallback behavior</li>
	<li>Check behavior on unsupported browsers/devices</li>
	<li>Test UI responsiveness and accessibility</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="DefinitionofDone"></a>Definition of Done</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Feature implemented and deployed to staging</li>
	<li>All acceptance criteria fulfilled</li>
	<li>QA sign-off completed</li>
	<li>No high or critical defects</li>
	<li>Documentation updated</li>
</ul>


<h3><a name="Comments%26TestResults"></a>Comments &amp; Test Results</h3>

<ul>
	<li>Multiple automated test runs resulted in <b>inconclusive</b> outcomes with all test cases blocked (visibility, SSO success/failure, Passkey fallback).</li>
</ul>

